========================================================================
PHASE-ORDERING STUDY (final DAG op-count vs pass order)
========================================================================

### abs( abs(x) * 1 )   [identity_op enables abs_abs]
    passes ['identity_op', 'abs_abs']: distinct final op-counts across 2 orders = [2, 3] | fixpoint = 2
    ORDER-SENSITIVE: YES
      best  2 ops: identity_op -> abs_abs
      worst 3 ops: abs_abs -> identity_op  (missed rewrite: an enabling pass ran too late)

### neg( neg(x) + 0 )   [add_zero enables neg_neg]
    passes ['add_zero', 'neg_neg']: distinct final op-counts across 2 orders = [1, 3] | fixpoint = 1
    ORDER-SENSITIVE: YES
      best  1 ops: add_zero -> neg_neg
      worst 3 ops: neg_neg -> add_zero  (missed rewrite: an enabling pass ran too late)

### abs( abs(x*1) * 1 ) [identity enables abs_abs, deeper]
    passes ['identity_op', 'abs_abs']: distinct final op-counts across 2 orders = [2, 3] | fixpoint = 2
    ORDER-SENSITIVE: YES
      best  2 ops: identity_op -> abs_abs
      worst 3 ops: abs_abs -> identity_op  (missed rewrite: an enabling pass ran too late)

### (x/1)**1 then neg(neg)  [disjoint patterns]
    passes ['div_by_one', 'pow_by_one', 'neg_neg']: distinct final op-counts across 6 orders = [1] | fixpoint = 1
    ORDER-SENSITIVE: no
